cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you cite a Bellwether result, cite the suite version, driver, agent, k and run seed alongside it - a number without those six coordinates is not reproducible.'
title: 'Bellwether: a reproducible reliability benchmark for computer-use agents on legacy enterprise software'
abstract: >-
  Bellwether measures whether a computer-use agent completes a task on every
  independent attempt from a byte-identical starting state, rather than whether it
  can complete it once. Trials fork a pinned snapshot, verdicts come from the
  application's own database rather than a language-model judge, every verifier ships
  fixtures proving it can fail, and a deterministic in-process simulator lets the whole
  suite run offline with no API key. It also compiles solved traces into deterministic
  flows and MCP tools, so the agent and the compiled flow can be scored side by side.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-03'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/al-mohad/bell-weather'
keywords:
  - computer-use-agents
  - benchmark
  - reliability
  - reproducibility
  - legacy-systems
  - robotic-process-automation
